Enhancement: Support `mount` on Windows

Restic `mount` was only available on Linux, macOS and FreeBSD. Restic now
also mounts a repository on Windows using WinFSP (https://winfsp.dev), which
needs to be installed separately. The mountpoint is either an unused drive
letter or a directory that does not exist yet, for example `restic mount X:`.

As colons are not allowed in Windows file names, the default `--time-template`
on Windows is `2006-01-02T15-04-05Z0700`. The `latest` entries are shown as
directories, and symbolic links or special files contained in a snapshot are
not shown on Windows.

